246
00:17:53,915 --> 00:17:58,699
Five mistakes to watch for. Each one
usually starts as a wish to be helpful.

247
00:17:59,039 --> 00:18:03,095
Switching to pull_request_target so
that fork pull requests get the key.

248
00:18:03,135 --> 00:18:07,703
Root cause: the trigger supplies the base
repository's secrets and token, and the

249
00:18:07,743 --> 00:18:10,889
checkout then executes the
contributor's code with them.

250
00:18:11,229 --> 00:18:16,384
Treating "we only read the prompts" as
safe. Root cause: test files, conftest.py,

251
00:18:16,424 --> 00:18:21,579
package scripts and templates that the
harness imports are executed, so data from

252
00:18:21,619 --> 00:18:23,503
the pull request becomes code.

253
00:18:23,843 --> 00:18:27,237
Putting models or anything
sensitive in the Actions cache.

254
00:18:27,277 --> 00:18:32,093
Root cause: anyone who can open a pull
request can read caches, and the size limit

255
00:18:32,133 --> 00:18:33,337
suits package caches.

256
00:18:33,677 --> 00:18:38,747
Using the production provider key for
evaluation. Root cause: one key then carries

257
00:18:38,787 --> 00:18:43,546
both the evaluation's exposure and
production's reach, with no spend ceiling.

258
00:18:43,886 --> 00:18:47,623
Exempting an agent's pull
requests from review or checks.

259
00:18:47,663 --> 00:18:52,991
Root cause: local hooks never ran for it,
so required checks and a human approval

260
00:18:53,031 --> 00:18:54,780
are the only controls left.

261
00:18:56,620 --> 00:19:01,754
Now, out of the lab. An open-source project
that maintains an LLM evaluation harness

262
00:19:01,794 --> 00:19:05,880
receives most of its prompt
improvements from outside contributors.

263
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:10,930
Its evaluation job fails on every one of
them. A contributor proposes the two-line

264
00:19:10,970 --> 00:19:12,408
change from the opening.

265
00:19:12,748 --> 00:19:16,807
The maintainer answers with the two boxes
of the diagram and then with a design.

266
00:19:17,147 --> 00:19:21,900
On pull_request, every contribution gets
the secret-free checks: lint, unit tests,

267
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:26,635
the repository's own check script, and the
evaluation against recorded responses.

268
00:19:26,675 --> 00:19:31,312
The paid evaluation runs in a separate
workflow that a maintainer triggers after

269
00:19:31,352 --> 00:19:36,222
reading the diff, with a provider key that
belongs to the evaluation alone and has a

270
00:19:36,262 --> 00:19:39,320
spend cap. The full suite
runs on main on a schedule.

271
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:44,172
The project's GPU machine isn't registered
as a runner for the public repository at

272
00:19:44,212 --> 00:19:44,406
all.

273
00:19:44,746 --> 00:19:49,910
The same maintainers later add an AI coding
agent. They apply the table: the agent's

274
00:19:49,950 --> 00:19:54,743
pull requests are small by instruction
and by a size check, they pass the same

275
00:19:54,783 --> 00:19:59,762
required checks, a human approval is
required by ruleset, the agent's token can't

276
00:19:59,802 --> 00:20:04,904
write to workflows, and its commits carry
a Co-authored-by trailer so that they can

277
00:20:04,944 --> 00:20:06,949
be listed with one git log query.

278
00:20:08,789 --> 00:20:15,860
